Output ONLY the C test function code. No explanations, no JSON, just compilable C code.

Generate a C test function for the following execution path.

FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: buffer_resize
Signature: int buffer_resize(buffer_t *self, size_t n)
Description: /**
 * @brief Resize a buffer to the specified size, rounded up to the nearest multiple of 1024.
 *
 * Adjusts the internal storage of the buffer to accommodate at least n bytes, rounding n up
 * to the next multiple of 1024. The buffer's memory is reallocated and a null terminator is
 * set at the end. Existing data may be preserved or lost depending on realloc behavior.
 *
 * @param self Pointer to the buffer to resize. Must not be NULL and must be a valid buffer_t.
 * @param n Desired minimum size in bytes. May be zero.
 *
 * @return Returns 0 on success, or -1 if memory allocation fails.
 *
 * @note Memory: Buffer memory is reallocated; caller must not use old pointers after resize.
 * @note Error: On failure, buffer contents may be invalid and should not be used.
 */
Dependencies: None

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION:
```c
